            <ArticleTitle>The foundation of sensory pharmacology: Nicholas (Miklós) Jancsó and the Szeged contribution.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>152-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/23328940.2015.1045683</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Capsaicin became an indispensable tool in pain research after the discovery of its unique pharmacological actions by Nicholas (Miklós) Jancsó Jr. in the late 1940s. This &quot;History Article&quot; introduces his achievements leading to the foundation of &quot;sensory pharmacology&quot; and subsequent research in that field at the University of Szeged, Hungary.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
